# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Adapting to Capability

How this project's output changes with what the environment can *do*, as distinct from how much
space it has. This is a fragment, not a standalone document role: paste it into whatever plays the
`patterns` role here — or into the responsive document's capability section, if that is where it
fits better — and fill in the `<!-- DECIDE -->` markers.

**Keep the two axes apart.** Available space and available capability vary independently, and
conflating them is the single most common mistake in this area: it produces layouts that assume a
narrow window implies touch, or that a large one implies a pointer. Neither holds. A narrow window
on a desktop has a mouse and a keyboard; a large tablet has neither.

If the material below grows past roughly a page, it has outgrown being a fragment — give it its own
document and link to it from both the patterns and the responsive documents.

